    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0371" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/7–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 213 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President and the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-12">12 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and top secret for the President and the Secretary of State from
                        Harriman.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>
                    Soong suggested to Stalin that he return to Chungking to consult
                    the Generalissimo over the points still at issue. Stalin however said that it was better to come to agreement
                    before he met you at Berlin as he wished to decide with you date of his entry
                    into the war. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
